# A program reading a module-private name it never bound — ouroboros#141,
# body repro 3.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that the splice used to make module state
# PROGRAM-VISIBLE: `counter` is _mod_priv's private global, and a program that
# reads it bare must die "undefined variable" as it does on the VM. Before
# the renamer the AOT printed 0 — a default-initialised C global, a plausible
# NUMBER rather than an error — rc 0, empty build log. With the module spliced
# under `_mod_priv__`, the bare name resolves nowhere, and both sides die at
# the same line with the same message (the `_err` class contract).
#
# The first print proves the module itself is live and its function still
# reaches its own state through the renamed binding.
import _mod_priv
print of (_mod_priv.bump of null)
print of counter
